              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Deut 23.25",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jesus was walking through some cornfields on the Sabbath. His disciples began to pick the ears of corn, rub them in their hands, and eat the grain. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.6.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.6.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 6:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Some Pharisees asked, “Why are you doing what our Law says you cannot do on the Sabbath?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.6.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.6.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
